[short_description:string]
EasyCharge is a platform for managing electric-vehicle charging networks, developed with a charging-solutions company to reduce dependency on third-party platforms. It uses a service-oriented architecture with OCPP for charger communication, a mobile app for drivers to locate chargers and manage charging sessions and payments, and a web admin panel for centralized network monitoring.

[description:md]
EasyCharge is a platform prototype for managing electric-vehicle charging networks, developed in collaboration with a client company specialized in EV charging solutions. The project responds to the company's need to scale its charger network while reducing dependence on third-party platforms, whose limitations constrained process automation, feature customization, and the user experience.

The solution is built on a service-oriented architecture that manages charging infrastructure, monitors charger status, and handles user charging sessions. Communication with physical chargers uses the **Open Charge Point Protocol (OCPP)**, while integrated digital payment mechanisms enable monetizing the service.

On top of this platform, the team built a mobile app for drivers—to locate chargers, manage charging sessions, and handle payments—and a web admin panel for internal staff to centrally monitor and manage the network.

The project followed a full software engineering process, from requirements gathering through architecture, development, and quality management, using agile methodologies (Scrum and Kanban). The result is a functional prototype that provides a solid technical foundation for evolving toward a production system.

